m.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T11:48:25-08:00","id":1367272,"title":"","content":"So stoked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T12:13:05-08:00","id":1367278,"title":"","content":"Reading through the antagonists, some really good stuff in here. Skimming through it I'm enjoying Chapter 2 more than Chapter 1.<br /> <br /> The extremely stylized, italicized, and tilted font on the letter in pg 79 is damn hard to read though.<br /> <br /> Update: the antagonists really shine. They're interesting and well thought through. Super interesting to see new base clans make an appearance. Out of curiosity, I wonder what guiding principles determine whether a concept gets a Bloodline with a new discipline, one with new merits, one with new devotions, or in this case, just forks to a whole new base clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 02-12-2020, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T13:29:39-08:00","id":1367292,"title":"","content":"sigh, it wont accept my credit card for some reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T13:46:46-08:00","id":1367296,"title":"","content":"A lot of varied ideas here. Skipping around at the moment but it all looks awesome. Definitely more of a Wicked Dead feel with the varied groups but it's nice that it's not 'just' vampire-likes and contains covenants. Definitely can use some of this stuff in non-vampire games but would spice up vampire stuff too. Love the cats and behold Belial's Brood, awesomely done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T13:57:21-08:00","id":1367299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spilled Blood p104</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Max lived a double life. He\u2019d hidden his affair with a Carthian harpy quite well, but her blood was taking a toll. When he finally diablerized her to truly consummate their relationship, it pushed his timeline up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you even call it love if you haven't literally eaten her soul yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:25:11-08:00","id":1367307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367299#post1367299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you even call it love if you haven't literally eaten her soul yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The term is called &quot;soulmates&quot; for a reason, yes. xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:48:10-08:00","id":1367309,"title":"","content":"I think the Bloodlines relied a <i>bit</i> too heavy on the crossover and previous knowledge (writers, I love you, but please, <i>explain what a Stigmatic is before putting in the Stigmatic-only bloodline)</i>, but everything else rocks! I want to play nearly all of the minor Clans (aka, all the ones who are playable) and I already love to hate Rampart and everything they made (and can I say how I love how they subverted the company being overtaken by a vampire because the co-owners are friends and one got genuinely concerned over his pal being Vitae addicted? Go Power of Friendship, even with the bad guys).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Amaranthine Cats are adorifying, and there is now a cell of lethal hunters in my game that is composed of mortal grannies who aren't in danger from their pale blood-eating babies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-12-2020, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:55:22-08:00","id":1367310,"title":"","content":"what can I do to have DRIVETHRURPG accept my card?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T15:02:08-08:00","id":1367314,"title":"","content":"Call your credit card company and ask them why it was declined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],