-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T15:40:59-08:00","id":1367323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367319#post1367319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Mikhailli's writeup mentioned that the all Clan has died by the Gangrel but a single member who went and spawned a Clan of his own- so maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's...actually rather clever. Could be they just mutated, not died. In this book, that's only thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T15:44:07-08:00","id":1367324,"title":"","content":"That's a super cute throwback if intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T16:15:10-08:00","id":1367326,"title":"","content":"BELIAL'S BROOD!<br /> <br /> I haven't read it, I wasn't even a fan of them previously, but I'm excited at having my mind changed maybe.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, because I'm curious: Why no more on Strix? I get why not the Sons of Phobos (Hi Thousand Years of Night), but I was looking forward to more Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-12-2020, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T17:16:52-08:00","id":1367339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367326#post1367326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BELIAL'S BROOD!<br /> <br /> I haven't read it, I wasn't even a fan of them previously, but I'm excited at having my mind changed maybe.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, because I'm curious: Why no more on Strix? I get why not the Sons of Phobos (Hi Thousand Years of Night), but I was looking forward to more Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>the strix make a apparence trust me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T18:26:51-08:00","id":1367349,"title":"","content":"Very much digging the book so far, but there's one thing nagging me a bit. I'm currently at the Belial's Brood section, and... they seem to be <i>really</i> hard up for Willpower, especially for a covenant whose Ritual Discipline burns it. Without Masks, Dirges, or Touchstones, unless they have one of a scant handful of merits they seem to only have the Inspired Condition and the surrender end of the Beaten Down Tilt to rely on. Well, and Aspirations, since they're probably only showing up at the table as storyteller characters in most circumstances.<br /> I'd believe it if told that they're designed to struggle with Willpower recovery, but still, that's kind of a major limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T18:39:35-08:00","id":1367351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367278#post1367278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through the antagonists, some really good stuff in here. Skimming through it I'm enjoying Chapter 2 more than Chapter 1.<br /> <br /> The extremely stylized, italicized, and tilted font on the letter in pg 79 is damn hard to read though.<br /> <br /> Update: the antagonists really shine. They're interesting and well thought through. Super interesting to see new base clans make an appearance. Out of curiosity, I wonder what guiding principles determine whether a concept gets a Bloodline with a new discipline, one with new merits, one with new devotions, or in this case, just forks to a whole new base clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for other writers, but it depends.<br /> <br /> I made the Bekaak a lost/minor clan because I felt like the archetype of age-sapping/entropic vampires was one that could stand on its own, rather than just a bloodline (they COULD be a bloodline, but I think they work as a clan too).<br /> <br /> The Hypatians were the idea of doing a Promethean-hybrid, and I didn't want to pin that on one of the big five. I also felt like vampires who self-embrace with alchemy should be their own thing.<br /> <br /> As for Disciplines vs. Devotions vs. Merits, I tend to go with Merits if they're more about enhancing powers rather than creating whole new ones, and Devotions if they're more variants on the core Disciplines. I do Disciplines if the power is a REALLY different idea than the basic ones.<br /> <br /> Also, on an unrelated note, is the errata form up somewhere? There are typos I'm responsible for that I've noticed... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:13:16-08:00","id":1367359,"title":"","content":"As a related note, the diseases mentioned are all cool.<br /> <br /> Well, okay, not cool, more like &quot;freakishly Lovecraftian&quot; (Nereids), &quot;John Carpenter's the Black Plague&quot; (Chimera virus) and &quot;AAAAAAAAAAH!&quot; (Blessing of Athena), but still awesomely disgusting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:17:14-08:00","id":1367361,"title":"","content":"Honestly\u2026I have to say I'm slightly disappointed. I loved every bit of <i>Bloodlines: the Devoted</i>, and so far <i>Spilled Blood</i> just hasn't thrilled me in the same way. It's not <i>bad</i>, but I'm probably not going to devour the whole thing in ten minutes.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue from my quick read, though, is the sheer number of new clans. In the entirety of 1e (if you ignore chapter 2 of the VII book) there were a grand total of two non-core clans (Akhud and Julii), and a big feature of Requiem as opposed to Masquerade was that clans were meant to be broad literary archetypes rather than &quot;this is the clan of Islam&quot; and &quot;this is the clan of body horror&quot; and &quot;this is the clan of snakes&quot;. But so far in 2e we've already got <b>ten</b> non-core clans, by my quick count (Jiangshi, Dukhan, Akhud, Julii, Mikhaili, Pijavica, Amari, Bekaak, Hypatians, Nhang). 1e had the issue of &quot;this is the bloodline of Nosferatu except they're cold&quot; and the like. Do we really need a whole <i>clan</i> of &quot;this is the clan of Gangrel except less solid&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:19:18-08:00","id":1367362,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for the answer Yossarian. Love your work, in general. <br /> <br /> Don't know if you know the answer but with the blood sorceries, was it a deliberate decision to abandon the themes and mechanics of Blood Sorcery? I noticed that wasn't a part of it like with SotC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:23:22-08:00","id":1367364,"title":"","content":"We're up to 20 clans if you include TY and DE stuff. Having said that it feels pretty clear that all but the core 5 are extremely rare or extinct. And they're super easy to convert to bloodlines if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:27:23-08:00","id":1367367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367362#post1367362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much for the answer Yossarian. Love your work, in general.<br /> <br /> Don't know if you know the answer but with the blood sorceries, was it a deliberate decision to abandon the themes and mechanics of Blood Sorcery? I noticed that wasn't a part of it like with SotC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't write up any of the stuff with rituals, so I can't really answer that. That being said, the SotC rituals are the only ones in 2E Vampire (I think) that explicitly refer to the themes from BS:S&amp;B, so it's more that that one book referenced them while others haven't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:28:25-08:00","id":1367369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367361#post1367361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue from my quick read, though, is the sheer number of new clans. In the entirety of 1e (if you ignore chapter 2 of the VII book) there were a grand total of two non-core clans (Akhud and Julii), and a big feature of Requiem as opposed to Masquerade was that clans were meant to be broad literary archetypes rather than &quot;this is the clan of Islam&quot; and &quot;this is the clan of body horror&quot; and &quot;this is the clan of snakes&quot;. But so far in 2e we've already got <b>ten</b> non-core clans, by my quick count (Jiangshi, Dukhan, Akhud, Julii, Mikhaili, Pijavica, Amari, Bekaak, Hypatians, Nhang). 1e had the issue of &quot;this is the bloodline of Nosferatu except they're cold&quot; and the like. Do we really need a whole <i>clan</i> of &quot;this is the clan of Gangrel except less solid&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, the new clans are all weird. None of them are like &quot;Gangrel, but less solid&quot;, and pretty much all of them have pretty weird tricks and thematics. Amari are angry ecologists and champions of endurance, the Bekaak are time-eating bluntly honest preachers, Hypatians are Promethean-hybrid alchemists and transhumanists, the Nhang are half-crocodile sea monsters, and the Twice-Cursed are a mistake. As in, they're something that wasn't supposed to be in universe and are trying to become a bloodline of the Daeva or Nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:34:09-08:00","id":1367372,"title":"","content":"Honestly the clans and BL write-ups had this feeling of &quot;hey this a showcase of all the variables and factors you can play with to make new esoteric vampire stuff yourself!&quot; I like how this feels like a demo for the system's flexibility. Would have loved a metawriteup about how to go from concept to mechanics with your own ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:36:01-08:00","id":1367373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367369#post1367369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and the Twice-Cursed are a mistake. As in, they're something that wasn't supposed to be in universe and are trying to become a bloodline of the Daeva or Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the Twice-Cursed should be so lucky. No, their fate is a lot more heartbreak, I'm afraid.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Stalkers aren't a clan. They're more like...revenants who are less <i>actively </i>screwed, yet damned in their own special way (especially if <u>anyone</u> figures out how they embrace). They could be a clan one day, but I'd say they'd have to kill a lot more vampires, and the Akhud are already filling that niche...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:41:04-08:00","id":1367374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367372#post1367372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the clans and BL write-ups had this feeling of &quot;hey this a showcase of all the variables and factors you can play with to make new esoteric vampire stuff yourself!&quot; I like how this feels like a demo for the system's flexibility. Would have loved a metawriteup about how to go from concept to mechanics with your own ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should definitely check out Rose Bailey's stuff on Storytellers Vault. She has lots to say about the meta-aesthetics and mechanics of Disciplines, and writing for <b>Vampire </b>in general.<br /> <br /> (excuse the double post)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:43:31-08:00","id":1367376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367351#post1367351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, on an unrelated note, is the errata form up somewhere? There are typos I'm responsible for that I've noticed... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I put it in the Thank You/Purchase Note as always. Check the receipt email or your Library.<br /> <br /> M","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T19:54:06-08:00","id":1367379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367376#post1367376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I put it in the Thank You/Purchase Note as always. Check the receipt email or your Library.<br /> <br /> M</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, much thanks! I totally missed it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:14:27-08:00","id":1367382,"title":"","content":"Also, while I think the Brood needs more Manifestations, I like them even better than their 1E version. They're simpler and less mystical, sure, but that's because they've been narrowed down to what was the best part about them - their complete acceptance of the Beast and complete peace with themselves and its urges. They aren't just ascended draugr, no, they're what happens when the Man and the Beast become equal partners who share the same opinions about things. Which means they're prone to some outright sympathetic motivations, but they're still inhuman predators, and gleeful ones at that. They've become the vampires other vampires tell ghost stories about, and they're fine with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:46:39-08:00","id":1367386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367369#post1367369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, the new clans are all weird. None of them are like &quot;Gangrel, but less solid&quot;, and pretty much all of them have pretty weird tricks and thematics. Amari are angry ecologists and champions of endurance, the Bekaak are time-eating bluntly honest preachers, Hypatians are Promethean-hybrid alchemists and transhumanists, the Nhang are half-crocodile sea monsters, and the Twice-Cursed are a mistake. As in, they're something that wasn't supposed to be in universe and are trying to become a bloodline of the Daeva or Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a bit better, but also\u2026is &quot;ecologist&quot; or &quot;preacher&quot; or &quot;bluntly honest&quot; or &quot;transhumanist&quot; really a feature of a clan? (&quot;Time-eating&quot; is, but that's their Discipline powers, I'm just thinking of the concept.)<br /> <br /> I like the core five because they're so broad and archetypal. Any of the five could be an ecologist or a bluntly honest preacher or a transhumanist. Which is just personal preference\u2014but it's why the extra clans don't generally interest me very much.<br /> <br /> I should clarify, I don't regret buying the book or anything, and it's not worse than TYoN or SotC or anything. I just had extremely high hopes after Devoted (my favorite Requiem book now), since I knew some of the same authors had worked on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:48:19-08:00","id":1367387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367382#post1367382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while I think the Brood needs more Manifestations, I like them even better than their 1E version. They're simpler and less mystical, sure, but that's because they've been narrowed down to what was the best part about them - their complete acceptance of the Beast and complete peace with themselves and its urges. They aren't just ascended draugr, no, they're what happens when the Man and the Beast become equal partners who share the same opinions about things. Which means they're prone to some outright sympathetic motivations, but they're still inhuman predators, and gleeful ones at that. They've become the vampires other vampires tell ghost stories about, and they're fine with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the old Brood, but I <i>really </i>like the new version. I don't recall who wrote them off the top of my head, but they did a really wonderful job. The 1E version being an international order of gnostic satanists was always a bit odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:31:50-08:00","id":1367437,"title":"","content":"Well, after reading DE2, I wonder how much of the former gnostic/statanist ideology is now covered by the Tenth Choir. I actually plan on giving it some very deep thought about how much of the old Brood can now be represented by a modern Choir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:47:48-08:00","id":1367449,"title":"","content":"....i am one of those assholes who see an everlasting and is like &quot;I WANNA PLAY ONE!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but sadly they are all so old! I want to play a new everlasting so i am not too op! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:51:12-08:00","id":1367450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367437#post1367437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, after reading DE2, I wonder how much of the former gnostic/statanist ideology is now covered by the Tenth Choir. I actually plan on giving it some very deep thought about how much of the old Brood can now be represented by a modern Choir.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I thought their Blood Sorcery being called &quot;Therion&quot; was a coincidence (it's just a Greek word for &quot;beast&quot;, and it shows up in occultism a fair bit), but now you're making me think it <i>is </i>a reference...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:05:20-08:00","id":1367452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367386#post1367386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is a bit better, but also\u2026is &quot;ecologist&quot; or &quot;preacher&quot; or &quot;bluntly honest&quot; or &quot;transhumanist&quot; really a feature of a clan? (&quot;Time-eating&quot; is, but that's their Discipline powers, I'm just thinking of the concept.)<br /> <br /> I like the core five because they're so broad and archetypal. Any of the five could be an ecologist or a bluntly honest preacher or a transhumanist. Which is just personal preference\u2014but it's why the extra clans don't generally interest me very much.<br /> <br /> I should clarify, I don't regret buying the book or anything, and it's not worse than TYoN or SotC or anything. I just had extremely high hopes after Devoted (my favorite Requiem book now), since I knew some of the same authors had worked on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is also my problem with most bloodlines. Any vampire can have an ideology. An ideology is not enough to base an entire clan or bloodline on. They should have something no other clan or bloodline has, otherwise they should be a mystery cult or mini-covenant, or just a thematic Merit. &quot;Ecologist&quot; is not a clan, it's a character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T02:19:24-08:00","id":1367457,"title":"","content":"Can someone please list the 10 bloodlines and their parent clans? I'll only be able to buy the book next week, but I'm so excited about the new bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:18:38-08:00","id":1367498,"title":"","content":"Ankou: Mekhet vampire cullers<br /> Icelus: Mekhet or Ventrue hypnomancers<br /> Jharana: Daeva with a special connection to the God Machine<br /> Liderc: Daeva who feed off human will<br /> Nosoi: Gangrel plague vectors<br /> Parliamentarians: Any, Carthian propagandist<br /> Penumbrae: Any, Crone diviners<br /> Scions of the first City: Any, Invictus city keepers<br /> Vardyvle: Ventrue with impossible aspirations<br /> Vilseduire: Daeva or Nossie debaucherers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:40:30-08:00","id":1367506,"title":"","content":"I probably missed something but the text says Ayanda gets most of her Vitae from ghosts but I can't figure out how or why that works. Do manifested ghosts have blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T06:42:40-08:00","id":1367521,"title":"","content":"Can anyone point me in the direction of more information on the Holy Engineers? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:03:23-08:00","id":1367524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367506#post1367506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably missed something but the text says Ayanda gets most of her Vitae from ghosts but I can't figure out how or why that works. Do manifested ghosts have blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Merit in the corebook that models vampires who are able to feed on supernatural beings. And it's especially good for lone wolf elders like her, because supernatural Vitae cheats feeding restrictions, she doesn't need to interact with Kindred for her fill.<br /> <br /> That Merit outright says that you can feed on ghosts, it's just unique to the vampire. I imagine for her, her body is able to reprocess plasm into blood, since it's explicit it looks like ectophagia to those who don't realize the ghost is fine afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:10:29-08:00","id":1367526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367524#post1367524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a Merit in the corebook that models vampires who are able to feed on supernatural beings. And it's especially good for lone wolf elders like her, because supernatural Vitae cheats feeding restrictions, she doesn't need to interact with Kindred for her fill.<br /> <br /> That Merit outright says that you can feed on ghosts, it's just unique to the vampire. I imagine for her, her body is able to reprocess plasm into blood, since it's explicit it looks like ectophagia to those who don't realize the ghost is fine afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm re-reading that now (Unnatural Affinity, p114). The merit is kind of confusing. It says in the description &quot;Each dot of this Merit allows your character to gain sustenance from one type of supernatural creature. This may mean werewolves, ghosts, mummies, zombies, or stranger things still.&quot; So ghosts are explicitly on the menu, but then it says &quot;For example, ghosts exist in an ethereal state, and don\u2019t have physical blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess my question was, what is mechanically required to use this merit on a ghost? Is being manifested enough? Do manifested ghosts have physical blood you can take? Is it 1-for-1 plasm for vitae? Or do you do corpus damage for vitae? Any of these would make sense, just trying to figure out what happens :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T08:29:37-08:00","id":1367540,"title":"","content":"The Brood section repeatedly mentions the Language of the Beast but doesn't at any point actually explain what this is (unless I totally missed it?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1456-zeke-hubris","name":"Zeke Hubris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:00:57-08:00","id":1367546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeke Hubris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367540#post1367540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brood section repeatedly mentions the Language of the Beast but doesn't at any point actually explain what this is (unless I totally missed it?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was mentioned a lot in their 1e book- some kind of &quot;unlanguage&quot; only the Brood can speak. Strange, however, that they don't explain it in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:02:06-08:00","id":1367547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367521#post1367521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone point me in the direction of more information on the Holy Engineers? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>They are in Danse Macabre, an optional covenant which deal with the God Machine and the Angel of Death from the Pain Prophet's Testament.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:46:33-08:00","id":1367553,"title":"","content":"I think the current pdf is supposed to be the advance copy -- does anyone know where to submit errata? I've noticed a couple typos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T10:19:45-08:00","id":1367560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367506#post1367506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably missed something but the text says Ayanda gets most of her Vitae from ghosts but I can't figure out how or why that works. Do manifested ghosts have blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, as others have mentioned, the Unnatural Affinity merit lets you feed on one type of supernatural and have their essentia count as Vitae for the purpose of feeding restrictions. If the chosen type is ephemeral, the merit includes knowledge of how to extract their Essence.<br /> <br /> (She also has multiple devotions involving ghosts that could help with this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T11:43:55-08:00","id":1367572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367553#post1367553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the current pdf is supposed to be the advance copy -- does anyone know where to submit errata? I've noticed a couple typos.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's linked in the email receipt from DTRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T12:00:06-08:00","id":1367575,"title":"","content":"I haven't read much apart from the new clans and Belial's Brood yet, but I wanted to get some thoughts down.<br /> <br /> The Amari are interesting, but the fact that they're so much like the previously mentioned Mikhaili is weird to me, especially as their write-up doesn't mention the other group at all. I like a lot about them and really want to use them, but I would have preferred if we got a proper version of Bereschligost instead of 'they just kind of have these helpful blood-conserving abilities at character creation with no cost', as it would have both given us a new Discipline and made them more in line with other clans.<br /> I have one Bloodline idea for the Amari, which would be a Bloodline that doesn't simply survive up in the cold north, but whose gifts allow them to control the ice and snow; their bane might be something like 'Cannot survive for long in too high a temperature' or 'Exert an aura of extreme coldness around themselves that they can never turn off'.<br /> <br /> The Bekaak are weird, but cool. I like that we actually have some unique Native American vampires now. I find it weird that their whole ageing situation isn't their bane, nor even related to their curse at all, but I suppose there are so many ways of turning back their ageing that it honestly seems more like a unique quirk than a particularly crippling curse; indeed, it seems like it might be to their benefit in a lot of cases, particularly their ability to give and take age.<br /> Vitiate is kind of odd, but its interesting. I do think there needs to be some clarification about whether the Discipline's Persistent effect can be turned off, though, because if not that might be a pretty serious double-edged sword.<br /> <br /> The Hypatians are my favourite, because they feel simultaneously unique and fill in a 'niche' that was kind of missing, being a more 'alchemical auto-urgic' kind of vampire. They feel the most playable and player friendly, easy to slot into things. I would have probably put their origins further back than the ninteenth century, but that's kind of filled in by one of their rumours suggesting that they might be older than they think.<br /> I want to make some Bloodlines for them. The two main ideas I have are a Bloodline whose gift uses their connection to Pyros to control mundane fire or electricity, as well as a more physically focused Bloodline that might take off of the 'Igor' archetype, a bit.<br /> <br /> The Nhang are very strange, as they're so much like Kindred and yet also kind of their own weird thing. I like that most of their deviations from the base Kindred template are represented as Devotions, rather than just being written as just a kind of thing inherent to them, like the Amari's abilities are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 02-13-2020, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T12:00:11-08:00","id":1367576,"title":"","content":"So while waiting for the next Hunter preview, let's give some reading for Spilled Blood-<br /> <br /> Ankou- I think I would have liked them better as a Covenant, serving as one of my seven faces of VII (the plot hook is right in there!)<br /> <br /> Icelus- two Anderson legends in the price of one for the OUaMD origin :P They fact they are also basically a Shadow Cult is also very cool.<br /> <br /> Jharana- Oh, I really like those! the Holy Engineers having a cameo is cool, and their origins and crossover with Demon are cool.<br /> <br /> Liderc- I have always wanted to see a liderc in the CofD, so now my wish was granted! Also- is that Mirror a reference for the Mirror from the Anthologies? <br /> <br /> Nosoi- I wonder what they would think of the Contagion<br /> <br /> Parlimentartians- not really of interest for me, being honest<br /> <br /> Pnumbrae- Ok, they are really cool<br /> <br /> Scions of the First City- they really feel like the Architects of the Monolith<br /> <br /> Vardyvle- creepy as hell<br /> <br /> Vilseduire- I like those<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood- they are cool, indeed, and I do intend on reclaiming their 1e philosophy and implement it to a modern Choir<br /> <br /> Esoteric Order of the Golden Star- while i like it that there is really no benefit of joining thise Covenant, it could have been cool if its actual members (those who knew it was fake) had some proficiency at crafting illusions and tricks that almost look like magic, but aren't. I wonder what would happen if they would manage, by any chance, to stumble upon some long dead Blood Magic.<br /> <br /> Kenora Coterie- Ok, that's disgusting <br /> <br /> Amari- So yeah, the Amari are without doubt connected to the Mikhailli. If them coming from around the same region, having the &quot;Northern Wars&quot; as a part of their background, the similarity with the Disciplines and the common nickname of the Winter Kings, their writeup outright mentions Saga's ability to preserve and survive on little Vitae, which is basically Breschligost. Perhaps Saga devoured the Gangrel who wanted to kill them and changed her Blood to become that of her enemies? Their special mechanics may very well be the remains of their original Discipline. While they may have also meant to replace the Mikhailli, and while the last were indeed undeveloped, it don't think it is fair to outright ignore their original writeup - even if the Amari's is really cool - and so I think it is better to include them both through the earlier theory.<br /> <br /> Ayanda- so she is something between a modern Mekhet and an Hollow?<br /> <br /> Bekaak- yeah, they are terrifying. Also, them being hunted by Cheiron to find the anti aging solution is HILARIOUS (not for them, of course)<br /> <br /> Hypatians- Ohhhhhh I really like those! Blood Chemistry also looks great!<br /> <br /> Nhang- Yeah, creepy as hell<br /> <br /> Amara- oh, poor thing<br /> <br /> Twice Cursed- yeah I am very interested in seeing them turning into an actual Clan<br /> <br /> Amaranthine Cats- oh, I LOVE the quote. Animal ghoul families was always a thing, and this exploration of it is just awesome, and immediately makes me think about the Cats of Ulthar. i also wonder about a crossover with the Colony.<br /> <br /> Blessing of Athena- even before reading it, I can bet it is nothing about a &quot;blessing&quot;. Yep. Not a blessing. Is it me, or that Vicissitude have managed to crawl its way into Requiem, souleaters/assaku and all?<br /> <br /> Blood Worms- Sure, because we didn't had enough of those monsters.... how many wormy parasites do vampires carry in their dead veins?<br /> <br /> Brotherhood of Blood- disgusting people using unoriginal names thinking themselves vampires. Oh, I just wait for them to meet some real vampires who will teach them a thing or two about blood and Blood.<br /> <br /> Chimera Virus- oh, wait, THIS is Vicissitude #The_Contagion_Ruins_Everything<br /> <br /> Everlasting- What. The. HELL?! This alone is worth the whole book (no offence to the rest of the awesome material in it)<br /> <br /> Heart's Bane- Oh, the poor, poor Bron.. Yeah, that's creepy<br /> <br /> Nereids- Sea, stop eating people and go back to sleep, you monster!<br /> <br /> Rampart Logistics- Yeah, that's gonna blow up SO BAD. If they'll survive long enough, they may become a conspiracy... if.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, a very nice read. A lot of cool material for both players and STs, and the new Clans are really cool. Nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T12:37:25-08:00","id":1367580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367575#post1367575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read much apart from the new clans and Belial's Brood yet, but I wanted to get some thoughts down.<br /> <br /> The Bekaak are weird, but cool. I like that we actually have some unique Native American vampires now. I find it weird that their whole ageing situation isn't their bane, nor even related to their curse at all, but I suppose there are so many ways of turning back their ageing that it honestly seems more like a unique quirk than a particularly crippling curse; indeed, it seems like it might be to their benefit in a lot of cases, particularly their ability to give and take age.<br /> Vitiate is kind of odd, but its interesting. I do think there needs to be some clarification about whether the Discipline's Persistent effect can be turned off, though, because if not that might be a pretty serious double-edged sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>The aging thing is definitely intended is a mixed benefit. Their real issue is less that they age and more that their Blood Potency can't get very high unless they spend a lot of time working on it directly, but even then, they can't spend more than [100 - Age at Embrace] years active without starting to get Cryptkeepery, though some Bekaak become senile enough that they don't really see that as a problem...<br /> <br /> (From a mechanical point of view, I wanted it to be a little easier for people to actually play them, while also adding a complication to chronicles that span decades.)<br /> <br /> As for why it's not their specific clan bane, there was some backstory text that unfortunately had to be cut which would've explained that a little better. Basically, they've always had the honesty problem, and the curse that makes them age has little to do with vampirism. That said, there are some who disagree:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Elders of the Tsihstekeri family, Ventrue natives to the same part of the world, say the Bekaak have always aged, and these Lords may have the weight of legend on their side. The Ojibwe tell stories about creatures called <i>bakaak </i>and <i>pau'guk</i> (poetically, \u201cskeleton\u201d), flesh eating monsters who were once warriors, cursed to prey on their former comrades. The Tsihstekeri hold an old grudge against the Bekaak, and would much rather see the Prophets put to rest than speak more truths. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-13-2020, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T13:38:10-08:00","id":1367595,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> if I may ask- are the Bekaak the Clan which were &quot;rigged by Dominate&quot; that you once mentioned? Them getting cheated by some dark power into becoming what they are now? As the Tsihstekeri are now Ventrue but were something else previously, I will not be surprised if they were those Bekaak who somehow avoided their second curse.. or maybe their slaves who rose to take their place. Both could serve as a cool stroy hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T13:42:48-08:00","id":1367597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367595#post1367595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a> if I may ask- are the Bekaak the Clan which were &quot;rigged by Dominate&quot; that you once mentioned? Them getting cheated by some dark power into becoming what they are now? As the Tsihstekeri are now Ventrue but were something else previously, I will not be surprised if they were those Bekaak who somehow avoided their second curse.. or maybe their slaves who rose to take their place. Both could serve as a cool stroy hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, maybe... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There's a little hint in there about how the Camarilla might've found &quot;like minds&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:21:51-08:00","id":1367605,"title":"","content":"Is the Nhang clan bane described correctly? The flavor text implies being out of water is a problem for them, but the only mechanical element described is vitae-below-humanity=more damage taken, with nothing about being on the surface or under water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:09:15-08:00","id":1367620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367605#post1367605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Nhang clan bane described correctly? The flavor text implies being out of water is a problem for them, but the only mechanical element described is vitae-below-humanity=more damage taken, with nothing about being on the surface or under water.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, that sounds like enough of a problem, since its caused by their skin drying out. That cannot be comfortable, even if it's not a dice penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:44:15-08:00","id":1367633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367620#post1367620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, that sounds like enough of a problem, since its caused by their skin drying out. That cannot be comfortable, even if it's not a dice penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My question is whether the flavor text is meant to have a mechanical implementation at all because it doesn't seem to? You could be low on vitae in or out of the water, so the last part of the clan flaw paragraph doesn't connect to the first part and I'm curious if something got omitted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-13-2020, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T17:46:28-08:00","id":1367653,"title":"","content":"I really dislike that neither the Ankou and Vilseduire seem to have a bloodline gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T18:30:27-08:00","id":1367658,"title":"","content":"Not really a big fan of antagonists books, but there are really good ideas along the way. Will totaly use the Liderc and the Nosoi. Amaranthine Cats and Everlasting are directly joining the cast of my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T00:31:17-08:00","id":1367698,"title":"","content":"And back at being a Vampire noob... can someone tell me where to find the Innamorata?<br /> <br /> (I like the book but it could use some references!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T00:52:59-08:00","id":1367699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367698#post1367698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And back at being a Vampire noob... can someone tell me where to find the Innamorata?<br /> <br /> (I like the book but it could use some references!)</div> </div> </div> </div>They were fist mentioned in the Daeva Clan book, IIRC, and get a writeup at Thousand Years of Night. They are the strange reincarnation of a vampire's most important people, and if the vampire drinks from them, they forget that they are dead and ends up walking into the sun or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T03:25:04-08:00","id":1367719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367524#post1367524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Merit in the corebook that models vampires who are able to feed on supernatural beings. And it's especially good for lone wolf elders like her, because supernatural Vitae cheats feeding restrictions, she doesn't need to interact with Kindred for her fill.<br /> <br /> That Merit outright says that you can feed on ghosts, it's just unique to the vampire. I imagine for her, her body is able to reprocess plasm into blood, since it's explicit it looks like ectophagia to those who don't realize the ghost is fine afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367526#post1367526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I'm re-reading that now (Unnatural Affinity, p114). The merit is kind of confusing. It says in the description &quot;Each dot of this Merit allows your character to gain sustenance from one type of supernatural creature. This may mean werewolves, ghosts, mummies, zombies, or stranger things still.&quot; So ghosts are explicitly on the menu, but then it says &quot;For example, ghosts exist in an ethereal state, and don\u2019t have physical blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess my question was, what is mechanically required to use this merit on a ghost? Is being manifested enough? Do manifested ghosts have physical blood you can take? Is it 1-for-1 plasm for vitae? Or do you do corpus damage for vitae? Any of these would make sense, just trying to figure out what happens :P</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367560#post1367560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, as others have mentioned, the Unnatural Affinity merit lets you feed on one type of supernatural and have their essentia count as Vitae for the purpose of feeding restrictions. If the chosen type is ephemeral, the merit includes knowledge of how to extract their Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unnatural Affinity quite clearly states that it alone does not provide the means for drinking from something that isn't physical. It's part of the drawback. If you take it as a player you need to work out how your character would do it with your ST, which could be anything from using Blood Sorcery to force Manifestations, to a Devotion to temporarily become ephemeral yourself, to just hunting in the Underworld where ghosts are already physical.<br /> <br /> Once finally getting a hold of a ghost, just use the standard rule: 1 Vitae per lethal damage dealt. Ghosts may not have <i>physical</i> blood, but nothing says they don't have ghost blood in their ghost bodies made out of ghost flesh. Just bite into that and drink.<br /> <br /> Not a single word is mentioned of converting fuel traits like Essence, or its byproduct Plasm, to Vitae. Maybe Ayanda does it like that (I don't have Spilled Blood yet) but it's not through Unnatural Affinity. Claiming that Unnatural Affinity says you eat their Essence is just false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-14-2020, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:49:00-08:00","id":1367923,"title":"","content":"So, the Nosoi have me wondering if Bloodlines should be tied to clans at all. Did we really need a Bloodline that was basically Morbus only much weaker? Was it only created because morbus are limited to Mekhet and someone wanted something similar for Gangrel? Where are the disease-oriented bloodlines for the Nosferatu, or the Daeva, or the Ventrue? Or is Nosoi meant to replace Morbus? With so many of the new bloodlines becoming milt-clan, covenant oriented, and even a couple not having clan restrictions at all, maybe all bloodlines should have their clan restriction removed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T09:40:52-08:00","id":1368054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367923#post1367923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Nosoi have me wondering if Bloodlines should be tied to clans at all. Did we really need a Bloodline that was basically Morbus only much weaker? Was it only created because morbus are limited to Mekhet and someone wanted something similar for Gangrel? Where are the disease-oriented bloodlines for the Nosferatu, or the Daeva, or the Ventrue? Or is Nosoi meant to replace Morbus? With so many of the new bloodlines becoming milt-clan, covenant oriented, and even a couple not having clan restrictions at all, maybe all bloodlines should have their clan restriction removed?</div> </div> </div> </div>some bloodlines are specifically mutative strains that focus the unique properties of a Clan's blood. so yes, it makes sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:08:46-08:00","id":1368142,"title":"","content":"Maybe I missed it, but does the book ever even explain what it means for a Bloodline to have Favored Attributes?<br /> <br /> I suppose it means that if you are Embraced directly into that Bloodline you choose your +1 Attribute from those Favored Attributes instead of those of your Clan, but I cannot be sure. Do they mean anything if you join the Bloodline later?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T16:33:01-08:00","id":1368168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368142#post1368142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed it, but does the book ever even explain what it means for a Bloodline to have Favored Attributes?<br /> <br /> I suppose it means that if you are Embraced directly into that Bloodline you choose your +1 Attribute from those Favored Attributes instead of those of your Clan, but I cannot be sure. Do they mean anything if you join the Bloodline later?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's for if you're Embraced into the bloodline; or rather, if you build a character from the start with that bloodline. Otherwise, a character joining later will have just had the standard Clan boost already, no extras. (Unless I'm totally misremembering, but I pretty sure that's how it works).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T17:28:32-08:00","id":1368178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368168#post1368168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's for if you're Embraced into the bloodline; or rather, if you build a character from the start with that bloodline. Otherwise, a character joining later will have just had the standard Clan boost already, no extras. (Unless I'm totally misremembering, but I pretty sure that's how it works).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have been nice if the book actually explained that.<br /> <br /> Same with bloodline Disciplines and what happens to your clan Disciplines after joining a bloodline. I managed to figure it out through common sense and asking a few developers, but it should have been covered in Spilled Blood.<br /> <br /> For those who are still wondering how clan Disciplines are handled after you join a bloodline: you keep your clan Disciplines and you can continue to buy dots in them, but if the Discipline isn't part of your bloodline, you have to pay the out-of-clan cost for it. Yes, that means that if you take the Parlementairian bloodline on a Ventrue, Gangrel or Nosferatu, you get to enjoy access to <b>three</b> unique clan Disciplines without needing to commit Amaranth or being taught by another Kindred. I guess the downside is a pretty hefty new Bane, but nothing a smart vampire can't handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T18:17:32-08:00","id":1368189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368178#post1368178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would have been nice if the book actually explained that</div> </div> </div> </div>The more I read through it, the more I enjoy Spilled Blood, but I agree that this being the first real reveal of Bloodlines should have spent some pagecount on talking about Bloodlines in general. The philosophy of them, the range of things they can encompass, and even the mechanics of joining them. It seems like the only glaring oversight in an otherwise pretty great product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T18:37:46-08:00","id":1368196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368189#post1368189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The more I read through it, the more I enjoy Spilled Blood, but I agree that this being the first real reveal of Bloodlines should have spent some pagecount on talking about Bloodlines in general. The philosophy of them, the range of things they can encompass, and even the mechanics of joining them. It seems like the only glaring oversight in an otherwise pretty great product.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> The core rule book has a short paragraph on bloodlines, but that was written way back when Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition was just new and the only information we had on bloodlines besides that was from the first edition and from some blog posts. The first edition and blog bloodlines didn't have Favored Attributes, so that part also wasn't explained in any of the material available back then. Now we have our first real second edition bloodlines and they seem to work a little differently from the first edition bloodlines, but we get no explanation or updated rules.<br /> <br /> The writing in Spilled Blood is A+, really good stuff, and I love the creativity that went into this book, but the QA department really dropped the ball on this one. The jury is still out on whether the game designers/developers also dropped the ball. My first impression is that the Belial's Brood game mechanics were never actually playtested before this book got published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T20:19:15-08:00","id":1368215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368196#post1368196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writing in Spilled Blood is A+, really good stuff, and I love the creativity that went into this book, but the QA department really dropped the ball on this one. The jury is still out on whether the game designers/developers also dropped the ball. My first impression is that the Belial's Brood game mechanics were never actually playtested before this book got published.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first impression is that they're antagonists, it doesn't really matter. Their defining ability is their ability to innately Ride the Wave, and that's pretty powerful without being game-breaking.<br /> <br /> And really, I don't think their abilities are at all broken either. They just need to have their Manifestation roll time shortened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T08:42:23-08:00","id":1368303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368215#post1368215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first impression is that they're antagonists, it doesn't really matter. Their defining ability is their ability to innately Ride the Wave, and that's pretty powerful without being game-breaking.<br /> <br /> And really, I don't think their abilities are at all broken either. They just need to have their Manifestation roll time shortened.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a Sorcery that relies on Willpower... while all their abilities to generate Willpower are stripped away from them... How is Belial's Brood going to get the Willpower to fuel their Triadic Evolution without a Mask, Dirge or Touchstone? <br /> <br /> Unless you use the optional rule where NPCs can regain Willpower by fulfilling Aspirations, there is no way for the Brood to ever regain Willpower and thus they can't ever use their Triadic Evolution sorcery. That's what is fundamentally broken about them. It also immediately disqualified them from ever being a playable option, which is a step back from first edition, where the Belial's Brood book made them a playable faction. <br /> <br /> <br /> On another note but still related to Belial's Brood's funky mechanics:<br /> <br /> Some of the Triadic Evolution rituals seem weak and pointless. Why would someone invest 8 Experience in 'Merely a Flesh Wound' and then go through the trouble of casting a ritual to ignore wound penalties for a couple of scenes, if you can get Iron Stamina, a Merit that costs only 3 Experiences and permanently allows you to ignore all wound penalties?<br /> <br /> Actually, why does Triadic Evolution exist as a fleshed-out sorcery system if Belial's Brood isn't meant to be playable? Does any Storyteller actually go through the trouble of rolling for NPCs casting rituals when the ritual doesn't directly target a player character? Am I the only ST who doesn't roll for NPCs unless it's strictly necessary? If Belial's Brood is supposed to be used as antagonists only, wouldn't it have been much simpler if Triadic Evolution was a group of Dread Powers the Storyteller can pick and choose from? Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T08:56:31-08:00","id":1368306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368303#post1368303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have a Sorcery that relies on Willpower... while all their abilities to generate Willpower are stripped away from them... How is Belial's Brood going to get the Willpower to fuel their Triadic Evolution without a Mask, Dirge or Touchstone?<br /> <br /> Unless you use the optional rule where NPCs can regain Willpower by fulfilling Aspirations, there is no way for the Brood to ever regain Willpower and thus they can't ever use their Triadic Evolution sorcery. That's what is fundamentally broken about them. It also immediately disqualified them from ever being a playable option, which is a step back from first edition, where the Belial's Brood book made them a playable faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they're not playable. They literally are draugr, they just happen to think in the long term. They do not have anything beyond their instincts and their hunger. So no, I fail to see how &quot;a sociopath who differs in that what's left of their Man is egging their Beast on is not playable&quot; is a flaw. Or a step backward, these guys are more frightening if they're a temptation and the absolute evil that seems so tempting to embrace.<br /> <br /> To be frank, I'm a Storyteller who rolls for antagonist action, and that gives a measure of tension; the longer you take, the closer you are to the Brood bringing forth their Manifestations and becoming even more lethal. The only flaw is, as mentioned, the range of Manifestations; a Brood member becoming a genius for one roll is genuinely a tension-building threat, because one roll is more than enough to, say, develop a perfect analysis of the structure of the domain. I just feel it needs to be shorter times between rolls for the sake of speed and because the only thing they're doing is flexing their evolved Beasts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T09:17:05-08:00","id":1368308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368306#post1368306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course they're not playable. They literally are draugr, they just happen to think in the long term. They do not have anything beyond their instincts and their hunger. So no, I fail to see how &quot;a sociopath who differs in that what's left of their Man is egging their Beast on is not playable&quot; is a flaw. Or a step backward, these guys are more frightening if they're a temptation and the absolute evil that seems so tempting to embrace.<br /> <br /> To be frank, I'm a Storyteller who rolls for antagonist action, and that gives a measure of tension; the longer you take, the closer you are to the Brood bringing forth their Manifestations and becoming even more lethal. The only flaw is, as mentioned, the range of Manifestations; a Brood member becoming a genius for one roll is genuinely a tension-building threat, because one roll is more than enough to, say, develop a perfect analysis of the structure of the domain. I just feel it needs to be shorter times between rolls for the sake of speed and because the only thing they're doing is flexing their evolved Beasts</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing &quot;of course&quot; about the Brood not being playable. They were made playable in 1e. So what they are intelligent draugr? How is that an argument against making them playable?<br /> <br /> And you're not addressing the point being raised. If you roll for the Brood, do you also track their Willpower? If so, how will your Brood NPCs earn back their Willpower without Masks, Dirges, and Touchstones? Through an optional rule for NPCs to gain Willpower for resolving Conditions or furthering Aspirations? It is a solution, albeit a bandaid solution, given how these rules are supposed to be <i>optional,</i> yet the Brood can't function without these optional rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:17:31-08:00","id":1368369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367576#post1367576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everlasting- What. The. HELL?! This alone is worth the whole book (no offence to the rest of the awesome material in it)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>highfive for everlasting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> beyond that 2 things<br /> <br /> 1. ....i wanna play one<br /> <br /> 2. MOAR STUFF NEEDED","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:51:39-08:00","id":1368383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368308#post1368308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is nothing &quot;of course&quot; about the Brood not being playable. They were made playable in 1e. So what they are intelligent draugr? How is that an argument against making them playable?<br /> <br /> And you're not addressing the point being raised. If you roll for the Brood, do you also track their Willpower? If so, how will your Brood NPCs earn back their Willpower without Masks, Dirges, and Touchstones? Through an optional rule for NPCs to gain Willpower for resolving Conditions or furthering Aspirations? It is a solution, albeit a bandaid solution, given how these rules are supposed to be <i>optional,</i> yet the Brood can't function without these optional rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but they weren't really fun in 1e to play. VII in all it's incarnations was more playable - and the argument against playability is the exact same as why you don't want to play one of the Rapt or Zi'ir; their very thematic runs counter to playing a sympathetic character, and they don't have the capacity to aim for things more than &quot;hunt, eat, sleep, repeat&quot;, they're just more eloquent about it. More than that, they raise themselves via fatal duels with each other; that's not exactly a way to have cohesive players.<br /> <br /> And I could raise the same point about spirits, who don't have Anchors either. Quite simply, the Brood can sleep too, and I find it thematic if they regain Willpower for their Persistent Beast Conditions - not to mention it's not actually said to be optional (I think the exact words were &quot;since NPCs don't have tracked Beats, they regain a Willpower in place of a Beat&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T15:06:02-08:00","id":1368411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368383#post1368383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, but they weren't really fun in 1e to play. VII in all it's incarnations was more playable - and the argument against playability is the exact same as why you don't want to play one of the Rapt or Zi'ir; their very thematic runs counter to playing a sympathetic character, and they don't have the capacity to aim for things more than &quot;hunt, eat, sleep, repeat&quot;, they're just more eloquent about it. More than that, they raise themselves via fatal duels with each other; that's not exactly a way to have cohesive players.<br /> <br /> And I could raise the same point about spirits, who don't have Anchors either. Quite simply, the Brood can sleep too, and I find it thematic if they regain Willpower for their Persistent Beast Conditions - not to mention it's not actually said to be optional (I think the exact words were &quot;since NPCs don't have tracked Beats, they regain a Willpower in place of a Beat&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to hear you didn't think it was fun to play a Forsworn character in 1e. I found the 1e version of Belial's Brood and roleplaying a character getting roped into the Brood plenty of fun. I'm probably not the only one who feels that way. In fact, I remember hearing many people say how the Belial's Brood book was perhaps one of the best books to come out of VtR 1e. Second Edition Belial's Brood feels like a step back from that.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Brood being evolved draugr now, but if that is the reason why they aren't a playable option now, then I'm not happy with them being evolved draugr, despite the idea being extremely cool on paper.<br /> <br /> As for NPCs, Beats, and Willpower, the exact quote is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In most cases, a Storyteller character doesn\u2019t need to gain Conditions, since the Storyteller doesn\u2019t earn Beats. She can simply roleplay the appropriate behavior or apply an appropriate situational modifier if circumstances demand it. However, a Storyteller character can gain Conditions occasionally, such as when a player character uses a supernatural power that inflicts one. If a Storyteller character resolves a Condition, she earns a point of Willpower for use in the same scene, instead of a Beat. </div> </div> </div>It's listed as an optional rule in a sidebar on page 76 of the Chronicles of Darkness blue book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T15:43:28-08:00","id":1368422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I could raise the same point about spirits, who don't have Anchors either. </div> </div> </div>Er... if I'm correctly parsing what you're referring to with this, spirits aren't a great comparison; they still get a point of Willpower per every three Essence they harvest, and a free point every day (page 127 of the <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>core under Advantages and Other Traits, respectively), and so don't really need Anchors the same way vampires do. That comparison especially stings since IIRC the Kindred aren't supposed to recover Willpower via Daysleep, so they don't even get a point per day. Easy fix via a simple houserule, but still... going Brood, player-intended or no, suddenly makes a vampire struggle more with Willpower recovery than just about <i>anything</i> that isn't an end-stage soulless mortal.<br /> Though that's a potentially interesting point of comparison, come to think of it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 02-16-2020, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T15:47:26-08:00","id":1368423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368383#post1368383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I could raise the same point about spirits, who don't have Anchors either. Quite simply, the Brood can sleep too, and I find it thematic if they regain Willpower for their Persistent Beast Conditions - not to mention it's not actually said to be optional (I think the exact words were &quot;since NPCs don't have tracked Beats, they regain a Willpower in place of a Beat&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits have Resonances that grant WP along with Essence as well as no powers that require WP expenditure.<br /> Vampire's don't get WP from sleep.<br /> NPCs getting WP instead of Beats isn't included in the VtR corebook; you'd need to be told about it or read it in one of the non-VtR books in order to import it to a VtR game, and CofD supplements are not supposed to require any books other than the specific game's corebook. (Also, the WP is only for the same scene. Coupled with the one Beat/scene rule, they'd never be able to gain more than a single temporary WP this way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T17:12:32-08:00","id":1368435,"title":"","content":"I feel as though I would be remiss to not bring up an important thing about vampiric Willpower recovery:<br /> <br /> The Inspired Condition \u2014 the Condition specifically recommended as a go-to pick for &quot;an exceptional success on a roll allows you to take a Condition&quot; \u2014 gives you a point of Willpower in addition to reducing the number of successes required to gain an exceptional success on a roll it's resolved with.<br /> <br /> The Predatory Aura applies one of three Conditions \u2014 the expressions of the Bestial Triad \u2014 that reduces the number of successes required to gain an exceptional success on a roll against a target.<br /> <br /> The Predatory Aura costs Willpower to fight (if you're a mortal or a vampire with lower Blood Potency), but lashing out itself doesn't cost anything to do.<br /> <br /> (Less consistently: exceptional success on frenzy resistance still refunds your spent Willpower +1, and the roll to ride the wave does not suggest that it works any differently in that regard.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T18:58:54-08:00","id":1368446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368435#post1368435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Predatory Aura costs Willpower to fight (if you're a mortal or a vampire with lower Blood Potency), but lashing out itself doesn't cost anything to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lashing Out always costs a Willpower when used against Kindred. You're right about defending, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T19:49:26-08:00","id":1368453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368446#post1368446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lashing Out always costs a Willpower when used against Kindred. You're right about defending, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I get for second-guessing my memory on a rushed post, I guess; I remembered the extra cost from the last time I made this observation, but scrambling through the Bestial Triad section only turned up the Fight cost and my eyes slid past the preceding section on the way out the door.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the answer to &quot;how does the Brood get Willpower?&quot; is very probably &quot;by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218397-advice-on-gauging-the-strengths-and-weaknesses-between-splats?p=1218507#post1218507\">Being</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1271662-how-wells-a-predatory-elder-work-for-a-session?p=1271678#post1271678\">Vampires</a>, same as the rest.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:28:01-08:00","id":1368477,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or are the Ankou a little anaemic? It feels like something vital was cut there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T09:08:18-08:00","id":1368540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1367575#post1367575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nhang are very strange, as they're so much like Kindred and yet also kind of their own weird thing. I like that most of their deviations from the base Kindred template are represented as Devotions, rather than just being written as just a kind of thing inherent to them, like the Amari's abilities are.</div> </div> </div> </div> What is their deal, anyway? They're clearly water-based, but how does that shake out in practice?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:42:55-08:00","id":1368568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368477#post1368477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or are the Ankou a little anemic? It feels like something vital was cut there.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a little boring for a bloodline, yeah, like a less interesting version of the Khaibit, from a gameplay perspective, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T18:02:43-08:00","id":1368655,"title":"","content":"Was there a reason why the Scions of the First City are so destructive? A fair amount of word count was spent talking about them being unpredictably dangerous. Like, I get that their powers are dangerous, but there didn't seem to be any elaboration about how or why the bloodline members would enact &quot;creation through destruction&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 02-17-2020, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T21:10:53-08:00","id":1368676,"title":"","content":"So, I'm mid-way through Chapter 3, and I have to say, well...<br /> Hello C\u0336h\u0336i\u0336m\u0336e\u0336r\u0336a\u0336 \u0336V\u0336i\u0336r\u0336u\u0336s\u0336 Vicissitude. Took you long enough to show up in VtR. Hopefully you don't come with a healthy dose of space demonic possession this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:59:09-08:00","id":1368945,"title":"","content":"Started reading through, Dead Signal discipline is <i>very </i>disappointing. Pretty much none of the powers there are worth 3xp, and would work better as a collection of merits. Or a complete discipline rewrite to write it up in a proper 2e style. As is, it reads like a disjointed mess of discipline from 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T10:04:22-08:00","id":1368963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368676#post1368676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm mid-way through Chapter 3, and I have to say, well...<br /> Hello C\u0336h\u0336i\u0336m\u0336e\u0336r\u0336a\u0336 \u0336V\u0336i\u0336r\u0336u\u0336s\u0336 Vicissitude. Took you long enough to show up in VtR. Hopefully you don't come with a healthy dose of space demonic possession this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>*points towards Athena's Blessing*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry to tell you it, but they are already here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:57:43-08:00","id":1369250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368963#post1368963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*points towards Athena's Blessing*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry to tell you it, but they are already here</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure. The Blessing seemed less... agressive and prone to weaponization, to me. Far from harmless, of couse, but you could almost feel a certain pity for its sufferers and the loss they felt after their ''babies'' were removed from them.<br /> Chimera, on the other hand, is straight up <i>The Thing</i>/[Tzimisce]-level in terms of unpleasantness and virulence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T00:36:37-08:00","id":1369296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1369250#post1369250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure. The Blessing seemed less... agressive and prone to weaponization, to me. Far from harmless, of couse, but you could almost feel a certain pity for its sufferers and the loss they felt after their ''babies'' were removed from them.<br /> Chimera, on the other hand, is straight up <i>The Thing</i>/[Tzimisce]-level in terms of unpleasantness and virulence.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, Athena's sacred bird is the owl, and as we all know, nothing good can come out of anything connected to owls..<br /> <br /> Now I must wonder what would happen if a vampire carrying the Blessing also gets infected by the Chimera virus. Now, that would be terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:29:31-08:00","id":1369401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1369296#post1369296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Athena's sacred bird is the owl, and as we all know, nothing good can come out of anything connected to owls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't made that connection, but that's <i>brilliant</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T05:37:15-08:00","id":1369564,"title":"","content":"For every 3 Amaranthine Cats in a pack their speed goes up by 10. The safe speed of a sports car (as per the core CofD book) is 140. 3*14=42, ergo three and a half dozen Amaranthine Cats in a pack can keep up with a sports car. Increase the pack size even more and they can keep up even at non-safe speeds. With enough Cats in one place and nothing will be able to outrun them.<br /> <br /> Nyoom!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T16:55:41-07:00","id":1385683,"title":"","content":"PoD goes live this Wednesday!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}